.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt CONSD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm consd
.Nd RavenBSD console server with a line discipline
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
registers the
.Dq tty:
scheme and serves one path,
.Dq console .
It owns the serial input line: a reader thread takes raw bytes from
.Sy DEBUG_READ ,
runs them through the line discipline and writes the echo back with
.Sy DEBUG_WRITE .
.Pp
In canonical mode
.Sy READ
returns whole lines terminated with a newline.
.Cm CR
and
.Cm LF
end a line, backspace (0x7f or 0x08) erases one byte, ^U kills the line, ^C discards it and
interrupts the pending read with
.Er EINTR ,
^D on an empty line returns zero bytes and ^L is inserted verbatim.
The line limit is 1024 bytes; further bytes ring the bell and are dropped.
In raw mode bytes pass through without echo or editing.
.Pp
A
.Sy READ
that finds no complete line waits until the reader thread has one or an event arrives; there is
no busy loop and no polling.
.Sy WRITE
writes the bytes to the console unchanged.
Several opens are allowed and reads are served first come first served.
.Pp
The mode operations travel over the S11
.Sy CALL
opcode as the 12-byte messages of
.Xr raven-proto-tty 3 :
.Cm SET_MODE
(mode, echo),
.Cm GET_MODE
and
.Cm FLUSH .
A mode switch drops a partially edited line, and
.Cm FLUSH
returns the number of discarded input bytes.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/consd.toml
Service manifest: needs
.Dq logd ,
provides
.Dq scheme:tty ,
readiness by scheme.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
runs until the process is terminated; it exits non-zero when the scheme cannot be registered or
the reader thread cannot be created.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr logd 8 ,
.Xr ramfsd 8
